WEBVTT

00:07.465 --> 00:09.175
[crickets chirping]

00:49.799 --> 00:51.926
[alarm blaring]

00:52.010 --> 00:54.471
[panting]

01:01.061 --> 01:02.187
[elevator descending]

01:09.027 --> 01:10.320
[elevator dings]

01:15.742 --> 01:17.494
[breathing heavily]

01:28.922 --> 01:31.299
[low growling]

01:35.136 --> 01:36.763
[screaming]

01:44.437 --> 01:48.149
[Mike] Something is coming.
Something hungry for blood.

01:48.233 --> 01:52.821
A shadow grows on the wall behind you,
swallowing you in darkness.

01:52.904 --> 01:54.864
- It is almost here.
- What is it?

01:54.948 --> 01:56.282
What if it's the Demogorgon?

01:56.366 --> 01:59.410
Oh, Jesus, we're so screwed
if it's the Demogorgon.

01:59.494 --> 02:00.537
It's not the Demogorgon.

02:00.620 --> 02:02.872
An army of troglodytes
charge into the chamber!

02:02.956 --> 02:05.083
- Troglodytes?
- Told ya. [chuckling]

02:05.166 --> 02:06.960
- [snorts]
- [all chuckling]

02:08.545 --> 02:09.963
[softly] Wait a minute.

02:10.630 --> 02:12.590
Did you hear that?

02:12.674 --> 02:14.092
That... that sound?

02:14.175 --> 02:16.845
Boom... boom...

02:16.928 --> 02:18.680
- [yells] Boom!
- [slams table]

02:18.763 --> 02:20.640
That didn't come from the troglodytes.
No, that...

02:20.723 --> 02:22.392
That came from something else.

02:24.853 --> 02:26.855
- The Demogorgon!
- [all groaning]

02:26.938 --> 02:28.398
- We're in deep shit.
- Will, your action!

02:28.481 --> 02:29.774
- I don't know!
- Fireball him!

02:29.858 --> 02:31.151
I'd have to roll a 13 or higher!

02:31.234 --> 02:33.069
Too risky.
Cast a protection spell.

02:33.153 --> 02:35.697
- Don't be a pussy. Fireball him!
- Cast Protection.

02:35.780 --> 02:38.491
The Demogorgon is tired
of your silly human bickering!

02:38.575 --> 02:40.368
It stomps towards you.

02:40.451 --> 02:41.452
- Boom!
- Fireball him!

02:41.536 --> 02:43.830
- Another stomp, boom!
- Cast Protection.

02:43.913 --> 02:46.749
- He roars in anger!
- [all clamoring]

02:46.833 --> 02:48.334
- Fireball!
- [die clattering]

02:48.418 --> 02:50.044
- Oh, shit!
- [Lucas] Where'd it go?

02:50.128 --> 02:51.838
[Lucas] Where is it?
[Will] I don't know!

02:51.921 --> 02:53.464
- Is it a 13?
- [Will] I don't know!

02:53.548 --> 02:54.716
[Lucas] Where is it?
[Dustin] Oh, my God!

02:54.799 --> 02:56.384
[Karen] Mike!
[Dustin] Oh, my God! Oh, my God!

02:56.467 --> 02:57.552
[Karen] Mike!
[Lucas] Can you find it yet?

02:57.635 --> 02:58.720
[Will] No, I can't find it!

02:58.803 --> 03:00.471
- Mike!
- [Dustin] Oh, my God! Oh, my God!

03:00.555 --> 03:02.348
Mom, we're in the middle of a campaign!

03:02.432 --> 03:04.559
You mean the end?
Fifteen after.

03:04.642 --> 03:07.812
[Lucas] Oh, my God! Freaking idiot!
[Will] Why do we have to go?

03:07.937 --> 03:10.607
- Mom, wait, just 20 more minutes!
- It's a school night, Michael.

03:10.690 --> 03:13.151
I just put Holly to bed.
You can finish next weekend.

03:13.234 --> 03:14.777
- But that'll ruin the flow!
- Michael--

03:14.861 --> 03:16.112
I'm serious, Mom.

03:16.195 --> 03:18.656
The campaign took two weeks to plan.

03:18.740 --> 03:20.658
How was I supposed to know
it was gonna take ten hours?

03:20.742 --> 03:22.619
You've been playing for ten hours?

03:23.953 --> 03:27.749
- Dad, don't you think that 20 more--
- I think you should listen to your mother.

03:27.832 --> 03:31.294
- [static crackling on TV]
- [grunts] Dang dumb piece of junk.

03:32.337 --> 03:34.297
[Will] Oh, I got it!

03:34.380 --> 03:36.257
- Does the seven count?
- It was a seven?

03:36.925 --> 03:39.469
Did Mike see it?
Then it doesn't count.

03:44.098 --> 03:45.266
[Dustin] Yo, hey, guys.

03:45.350 --> 03:47.227
- Does anyone want this?
- [both] No.

03:50.688 --> 03:51.856
[Nancy] Yeah.

03:52.649 --> 03:54.234
No, I don't think...

03:55.360 --> 03:56.945
Yeah, he's cute.

03:57.028 --> 04:00.365
Barb, no, I don't think so.

04:00.448 --> 04:01.908
- Barb, you're not--
- Hey, Nancy.

04:02.784 --> 04:04.160
There's a slice left if you want it.

04:04.244 --> 04:06.579
- Sausage and pepperoni!
- Hold on.

04:13.461 --> 04:17.382
- There's something wrong with your sister.
- What are you talking about?

04:17.465 --> 04:19.259
- She's got a stick up her butt.
- [Lucas] Yeah.

04:19.342 --> 04:21.844
It's because she's been dating
that douchebag, Steve Harrington.

04:21.928 --> 04:23.680
[Dustin] Yeah,
she's turning into a real jerk.

04:23.763 --> 04:25.098
She's always been a real jerk.

04:25.181 --> 04:27.058
Nuh-uh, she used to be cool.

04:27.141 --> 04:29.519
Like that time she dressed up as an elf
for our Elder tree campaign.

04:29.602 --> 04:30.812
[Mike] Four years ago!

04:30.937 --> 04:32.355
[Dustin] Just saying.
[Lucas] Later.

04:33.940 --> 04:35.984
- It was a seven.
- Huh?

04:36.067 --> 04:37.819
The roll, it was a seven.

04:38.903 --> 04:41.114
The Demogorgon, it got me.

04:42.490 --> 04:44.158
[grunts] See you tomorrow.

04:59.799 --> 05:02.844
[Lucas] Good night, ladies.
[Dustin] Kiss your mom 'night for me.

05:04.178 --> 05:06.264
Race you back to my place?
Winner gets a comic.

05:06.347 --> 05:08.016
- Any comic?
- Yeah.

05:08.891 --> 05:11.019
[Dustin] Hey! Hey!

05:11.102 --> 05:13.062
I didn't say "go"!

05:15.106 --> 05:17.150
Get back here!

05:17.233 --> 05:19.360
I'm gonna kill you!

05:19.444 --> 05:21.863
[Will] I'll take your X-Men 134!

05:28.161 --> 05:29.704
Son of a bitch.

05:54.479 --> 05:55.521
[gasps]

05:57.815 --> 05:59.150
[grunts]

06:00.359 --> 06:01.652
[whimpers]

06:05.031 --> 06:06.783
[indistinct growling]

06:07.784 --> 06:09.452
[gasps]

06:16.667 --> 06:18.669
[Will panting]

06:23.883 --> 06:25.218
[dog barking]

06:28.763 --> 06:30.139
Mom?

06:30.223 --> 06:32.767
- Jonathan? Mom?
- [barking continues]

06:41.275 --> 06:44.362
[indistinct screeching]

06:50.618 --> 06:51.994
[line ringing]

06:54.705 --> 06:57.416
- Hello? Hello?
- [static crackling]

06:57.500 --> 06:59.127
[indistinct screeching]

06:59.210 --> 07:00.545
[barking]

07:02.713 --> 07:04.382
[whimpering]

07:05.842 --> 07:07.093
[growling]

07:13.349 --> 07:15.852
- [dial tone]
- [barking continues]

07:29.657 --> 07:31.576
[panting]

07:48.384 --> 07:50.094
[breathing shakily]

07:56.726 --> 07:59.061
[growling]

08:01.105 --> 08:03.024
[indistinct screeching]

08:07.028 --> 08:08.988
[screeching intensifies]

08:12.992 --> 08:14.285
[screeching stops]

08:25.922 --> 08:27.924
[theme music playing]

09:27.942 --> 09:30.027
[indistinct chatter on TV]

09:30.111 --> 09:32.405
[woman on TV] And that's it
for News Center this morning.

09:32.488 --> 09:33.823
Thanks for joining us.

09:33.906 --> 09:36.200
Let's hand off now to Liz
at the news desk.

09:36.284 --> 09:37.702
[Liz] All right, thank you, Donna.

09:37.785 --> 09:38.869
Turning now to local news,

09:38.953 --> 09:42.373
we're getting reports of surges
and power outages all across the county.

09:42.456 --> 09:45.418
Last night, hundreds of homes
in East Hawkins were affected,

09:45.501 --> 09:47.878
leaving many residents in the dark.

09:47.962 --> 09:50.089
The cause of the outage is still unknown.

09:50.172 --> 09:52.383
We reached out to Roane County
Water and Electric,

09:52.466 --> 09:55.011
and a spokesperson says
that they are confident

09:55.094 --> 09:57.680
power will be restored
to all remaining homes

09:57.763 --> 09:59.307
within the next several hours.

09:59.390 --> 10:01.142
[news continues indistinctly]

10:01.225 --> 10:02.643
- [dog barking]
- [snorts]

10:03.769 --> 10:05.062
[sighs]

10:08.274 --> 10:09.400
- [groans]
- [watch beeps]

10:16.115 --> 10:17.700
[lighter flicks]

10:20.870 --> 10:23.581
[inhales and exhales deeply]

10:25.875 --> 10:27.043
Mmm.

10:33.591 --> 10:34.592
[groans]

10:46.687 --> 10:47.730
[exhales]

10:47.813 --> 10:48.856
[sighs]

10:58.491 --> 11:00.701
In other news,
you might wanna stay home tonight

11:00.785 --> 11:02.078
or at least pack an umbrella.

11:02.161 --> 11:04.580
We turn to everybody's favorite
morning weather guy, Charles.

11:04.664 --> 11:06.999
[birds chirping]

11:09.085 --> 11:11.087
[Joyce] Where the hell are they?

11:11.170 --> 11:13.589
- Jonathan?
- Check the couch!

11:13.672 --> 11:14.799
Ugh, I did.

11:15.925 --> 11:18.386
Oh... Got them.

11:19.512 --> 11:21.847
Okay, sweetie, I will see you tonight.

11:21.931 --> 11:23.766
- Yeah, see you later.
- Where's Will?

11:23.849 --> 11:24.934
Oh, I didn't get him up yet.

11:25.017 --> 11:26.143
- He's probably still sleeping.
- [sighs]

11:26.227 --> 11:29.355
- Jonathan, you have to make sure he's up!
- Mom, I'm making breakfast.

11:29.438 --> 11:31.273
I told you this a thousand times.

11:31.357 --> 11:34.985
Will! Come on, honey.
It's time to get up.

11:38.364 --> 11:41.742
- He came home last night, right?
- He's not in his room?

11:41.826 --> 11:44.120
- Did he come home or not?
- I don't know.

11:44.203 --> 11:45.454
- You don't know?
- No.

11:45.538 --> 11:47.581
[stammering] I got home late.
I was working.

11:47.665 --> 11:48.707
You were working?

11:48.791 --> 11:50.709
Eric asked if I could cover.
I said yeah.

11:50.793 --> 11:52.253
I just thought we could use
the extra cash.

11:52.336 --> 11:55.047
- Jonathan, we've talked about this.
- I know, I know.

11:55.131 --> 11:57.049
You can't take shifts when I'm working.

11:57.133 --> 11:59.301
Mom, it's not a big deal.
Look, he was at the Wheelers' all day.

11:59.385 --> 12:02.054
- I'm sure he just stayed over.
- [sighs] I can't believe you.

12:02.138 --> 12:04.723
I can't believe you sometimes.

12:07.810 --> 12:11.272
- [phone ringing]
- That's disgusting.

12:11.355 --> 12:13.566
- [Mike] You're disgusting!
- Hello?

12:13.649 --> 12:15.401
Hi, Karen.
It's Joyce.

12:15.484 --> 12:17.528
- [Karen] Oh, Joyce, hi.
- What the hell, Mike?

12:17.611 --> 12:18.779
- [Ted] Hey!
- Quiet!

12:18.863 --> 12:20.573
- Language.
- Are you kidding?

12:20.656 --> 12:22.032
Was that Will I heard back there?

12:22.116 --> 12:23.617
Will?
No, no, no, it's just Mike.

12:23.701 --> 12:25.119
Will didn't spend the night?

12:25.202 --> 12:27.621
[Karen] No, he left here
a little bit after 8:00.

12:27.705 --> 12:29.039
Why? He's not home?

12:29.123 --> 12:32.960
Um, you know what? I think
he just left early for... for school.

12:33.043 --> 12:35.045
- Thank you so much. Bye.
- Okay. Bye.

12:52.980 --> 12:54.398
[school bell ringing]

12:57.109 --> 12:59.904
That's weird.
I don't see him.

12:59.987 --> 13:01.530
[Lucas] I'm telling you, his mom's right.

13:01.614 --> 13:03.449
He probably just
went to class early again.

13:03.532 --> 13:06.035
Yeah, he's always paranoid
Gursky's gonna give him another pop quiz.

13:06.118 --> 13:08.037
Step right up, ladies and gentlemen.

13:08.871 --> 13:11.373
Step right up and get your tickets
for the freak show.

13:11.457 --> 13:14.084
Who do you think would make more money
in a freak show?

13:15.836 --> 13:19.757
Midnight, Frogface, or Toothless?

13:20.799 --> 13:22.009
[sighs]

13:23.511 --> 13:25.346
[mimicking Dustin]
I'd go with Toothless.

13:25.429 --> 13:28.891
I told you a million times,
my teeth are coming in.

13:28.974 --> 13:30.726
It's called cleidocranial dysplasia.

13:30.809 --> 13:32.811
[mimicking Dustin]
"I told you a million times."

13:32.895 --> 13:34.939
- [chuckles]
- Do the arm thing.

13:35.731 --> 13:37.066
Do it, freak!

13:40.945 --> 13:43.322
- [bones cracking]
- [both groaning]

13:43.405 --> 13:45.658
[Troy] God, it gets me every time.

13:46.951 --> 13:49.828
- Assholes.
- [Mike] I think it's kinda cool.

13:49.912 --> 13:52.081
It's like you have superpowers
or something.

13:52.164 --> 13:54.041
Like Mr. Fantastic.

13:54.124 --> 13:56.377
[Dustin] Yeah,
except I can't fight evil with it.

14:00.923 --> 14:03.467
[bell ringing]

14:04.677 --> 14:06.512
[Barbara] So, did he call?

14:06.595 --> 14:09.139
Keep your voice down.

14:09.223 --> 14:10.808
Did he?

14:10.891 --> 14:12.643
I told you, it's not like that.

14:13.227 --> 14:16.981
Okay, I mean, yes, he likes me,
but not like that.

14:17.690 --> 14:18.983
We just...

14:20.109 --> 14:21.610
made out a couple times.

14:21.694 --> 14:25.072
"We just... made out a couple times."

14:25.155 --> 14:26.490
Nance, seriously,

14:26.574 --> 14:28.659
you're gonna be so cool now,
it's ridiculous.

14:28.742 --> 14:30.160
No, I'm not.

14:30.244 --> 14:33.914
You better still hang out with me,
that's all I'm saying.

14:33.998 --> 14:36.792
If you become friends with Tommy H.
or Carol--

14:36.876 --> 14:38.168
Oh, that's gross!

14:38.252 --> 14:40.421
Okay,
I'm telling you, it was a one-time...

14:41.255 --> 14:43.340
- Two-time thing.
- [chuckles]

14:48.178 --> 14:49.471
You were saying?

14:59.899 --> 15:01.358
- Steve...
- Mmm-hmm?

15:01.442 --> 15:03.110
- I have to go.
- In a minute.

15:03.193 --> 15:04.486
[bell ringing]

15:04.570 --> 15:06.864
Steve.
I really, like...

15:06.947 --> 15:08.782
Seriously, I have to go.

15:08.866 --> 15:10.242
Wait, wait, wait.
Let's...

15:10.326 --> 15:12.202
Come on, let's do something tonight, yeah?

15:12.286 --> 15:15.205
Uh... No, I can't.
I have to study for Kaminsky's test.

15:15.289 --> 15:17.541
Oh, come on.
What's your GPA again? 3.999...

15:17.625 --> 15:19.335
Kaminsky's tests are impossible.

15:19.418 --> 15:21.587
- Well, then, just let me help.
- You failed chem.

15:21.670 --> 15:23.672
- C-minus.
- Well, in that case...

15:23.756 --> 15:26.091
So I'll be over around, say, like, 8:00?

15:26.175 --> 15:29.136
- Are you crazy? My mom would not--
- I'll climb through your window.

15:29.219 --> 15:31.388
She won't even know I'm there.
I'm stealthy, like a ninja.

15:31.472 --> 15:32.723
You are crazy.

15:32.806 --> 15:34.642
Wait, wait, wait. Just...
Okay, forget about that.

15:34.725 --> 15:36.018
We can just...

15:36.101 --> 15:38.020
We can just, like, chill in my car.

15:38.103 --> 15:41.065
We can find
a nice quiet place to park, and...

15:41.148 --> 15:44.568
Steve... I have to study.

15:44.652 --> 15:46.362
I'm not kidding.

15:46.445 --> 15:48.739
Well, why do you think
I want it to be nice and quiet?

15:50.616 --> 15:52.493
You're an idiot, Steve Harrington.

15:52.576 --> 15:54.119
[sighs]

15:58.457 --> 16:01.043
Meet me at Dearborn and Maple at 8:00.

16:01.877 --> 16:03.253
To study.

16:06.507 --> 16:08.425
[bell ringing]

16:16.475 --> 16:17.768
Good of you to show.

16:17.851 --> 16:21.522
[Hopper slurring] Oh, hey, morning, Flo.
Morning, everybody.

16:21.605 --> 16:25.275
- Hey, Chief.
- Damn! You look like hell, Chief.

16:25.359 --> 16:26.360
- Oh, yeah?
- [chuckles] Yeah.

16:26.443 --> 16:28.988
Well, I looked better than your wife
when I left her this morning.

16:29.071 --> 16:30.072
[officers laughing]

16:30.155 --> 16:31.699
While you were drinking or sleeping,

16:31.782 --> 16:34.743
or whatever it is you deemed
so necessary on Monday morning,

16:34.827 --> 16:35.828
Phil Larson called.

16:35.911 --> 16:38.580
Said some kids are stealing
the gnomes out of his garden again.

16:38.664 --> 16:40.124
Oh, those garden gnomes again.

16:40.207 --> 16:42.459
Well, I'll tell you what,
I'm gonna get right on that.

16:42.543 --> 16:44.086
On a more pressing matter,

16:44.169 --> 16:46.213
Joyce Byers can't find her son
this morning.

16:46.296 --> 16:49.049
[muffled] Mmm.
Okay, I'm gonna get on that.

16:49.133 --> 16:51.343
- Just give me a minute.
- Joyce is very upset.

16:51.427 --> 16:53.303
Well, Flo, Flo, we've discussed this.

16:53.387 --> 16:55.723
Mornings are for coffee and contemplation.

16:55.806 --> 16:59.685
- Chief, she's already in your--
- Coffee and contemplation, Flo!

17:10.154 --> 17:12.948
I have been waiting here
over an hour, Hopper.

17:13.032 --> 17:15.617
[sighs deeply] And I apologize again.

17:15.701 --> 17:17.077
I'm going out of my mind!

17:17.161 --> 17:20.748
Look, boy his age,
he's probably just playing hookie, okay?

17:20.831 --> 17:22.833
No, not my Will.
He's not like that.

17:22.916 --> 17:24.460
- He wouldn't do that.
- Well, you never know.

17:24.543 --> 17:26.253
I mean, my mom thought
I was on the debate team,

17:26.336 --> 17:27.921
when really I was just screwing
Chrissy Carpenter

17:28.005 --> 17:29.673
in the back of my dad's Oldsmobile, so...

17:29.757 --> 17:32.718
Look, he's not like you, Hopper.
He's not like me.

17:32.801 --> 17:35.304
He's not like... most.

17:35.387 --> 17:39.266
He has a couple of friends,
but, you know, the kids, they're mean.

17:39.349 --> 17:41.185
They make fun of him.
They call him names.

17:41.268 --> 17:43.312
- They laugh at him, his clothes--
- His clothes?

17:43.395 --> 17:45.355
- What's wrong with his clothes?
- I don't know.

17:45.439 --> 17:47.733
- Does that matter?
- Maybe.

17:47.816 --> 17:50.861
Look, he's...
He's a sensitive kid.

17:50.944 --> 17:54.656
Lonnie... [sighs]
Lonnie used to say he was queer.

17:54.740 --> 17:56.075
[softy] Called him a fag.

17:56.158 --> 18:00.079
- Is he?
- He's missing is what he is.

18:01.580 --> 18:03.957
When was the last time
you heard from Lonnie?

18:04.041 --> 18:05.084
[scoffs]

18:06.085 --> 18:10.422
Uh, last I heard, he was in Indianapolis.
That was about a year ago.

18:10.506 --> 18:13.258
- But he has nothing to do with this.
- Why don't you give me his number?

18:13.342 --> 18:15.219
You know, Hopper,
he has nothing to do with this. Trust me.

18:15.302 --> 18:18.514
Joyce, 99 out of 100 times,
kid goes missing,

18:18.597 --> 18:20.724
the kid is with a parent or relative.

18:20.808 --> 18:22.309
[stammers] What about the other time?

18:22.392 --> 18:25.729
- What?
- You said, "99 out of 100."

18:25.854 --> 18:27.856
- What about the other time, the one?
- Joyce.

18:27.940 --> 18:29.066
The one!

18:29.149 --> 18:30.984
- Joyce, this is Hawkins, okay?
- [sighs]

18:31.068 --> 18:32.820
You wanna know the worst thing
that's ever happened here

18:32.903 --> 18:33.987
in the four years I've been working here?

18:34.071 --> 18:35.239
Do you wanna know the worst thing?

18:35.322 --> 18:38.450
It was when an owl attacked
Eleanor Gillespie's head

18:38.534 --> 18:40.244
because it thought
that her hair was a nest.

18:40.327 --> 18:42.996
Okay, fine.
I will call Lonnie.

18:43.080 --> 18:44.790
He will talk to me before he talks to--

18:44.873 --> 18:46.834
- What, a pig?
- A cop!

18:47.918 --> 18:50.921
[voice breaking] Just find my son, Hop.

18:51.004 --> 18:52.881
Find him!

19:04.476 --> 19:05.644
[man] Dr. Brenner.

19:07.604 --> 19:09.273
[scientist] This way, gentlemen.

19:09.356 --> 19:12.192
The entire east wing
will be evacuated within the hour.

19:12.276 --> 19:16.113
We've sealed off this area
following quarantine protocol.

19:23.829 --> 19:24.955
[air hissing]

19:35.549 --> 19:37.176
[guns cocking]

19:38.510 --> 19:40.929
[elevator humming]

19:49.104 --> 19:51.064
[elevator thuds]

20:33.273 --> 20:35.984
[squelching]

20:43.492 --> 20:44.660
[low growling]

20:56.546 --> 20:58.548
[indistinct growling]

21:02.302 --> 21:04.930
[man 1] This is where it came from?
[man 2] Yes.

21:05.013 --> 21:06.014
[man 1] And the girl?

21:07.641 --> 21:09.768
She can't have gone far.

21:12.312 --> 21:13.605
[growls]

21:46.430 --> 21:48.432
[music playing faintly]

22:03.030 --> 22:04.740
[Ben] All right, and one more.

22:05.699 --> 22:07.617
[man] Hey, Ben.
What do you think about that, uh...

22:07.701 --> 22:09.244
Hey, I don't know.
I don't know.

22:09.328 --> 22:11.663
[man] I don't know,
37 points per game average--

22:11.747 --> 22:13.457
[Ben] Thirty-seven now, but...
[man] Mr. Basket.

22:33.185 --> 22:36.063
[indistinct chatter]

22:43.612 --> 22:45.113
Hey!

22:45.197 --> 22:46.323
Come here!

22:47.074 --> 22:48.366
Hey, come here!

22:53.038 --> 22:55.082
You think you can steal from me, boy?

22:57.584 --> 22:58.752
What in the hell?

23:00.295 --> 23:03.131
- [bell ringing]
- [Mr. Clarke] Remember, finish chapter 12

23:03.215 --> 23:07.010
and answer 12.3 on the difference
between an experiment

23:07.094 --> 23:09.221
and other forms of science investigation.

23:09.304 --> 23:13.183
This will be on the test,
which will cover chapters 10 through 12.

23:13.266 --> 23:16.311
[trailing off] It will be multiple choice
with an essay section.

23:17.979 --> 23:19.356
So, did it come?

23:19.439 --> 23:20.816
Sorry, boys.

23:20.899 --> 23:22.776
I hate to be the bearer of bad news,
but...

23:23.985 --> 23:24.903
it came.

23:28.490 --> 23:29.491
Yes!

23:29.574 --> 23:31.368
The Heathkit ham shack.

23:31.451 --> 23:32.911
[Mike] Whoa.
[Mr. Clarke] Ain't she a beaut?

23:32.994 --> 23:35.038
I bet you can talk to New York
on this thing.

23:35.122 --> 23:36.289
Think bigger.

23:36.373 --> 23:38.375
- California?
- Bigger.

23:38.458 --> 23:39.835
Australia?

23:40.794 --> 23:42.379
- [boys exclaiming]
- [Lucas] Oh, man!

23:42.462 --> 23:45.340
When Will sees this,
he's totally gonna blow his shit.

23:45.423 --> 23:46.508
Lucas!

23:46.591 --> 23:47.968
- Sorry.
- [Dustin chuckles]

23:49.261 --> 23:50.428
[radio tuning]

23:50.512 --> 23:52.931
[in Australian accent]
Hello, this is Mike Wheeler,

23:53.014 --> 23:55.725
president of Hawkins Middle AV Club.

23:57.269 --> 23:58.478
[Lucas] What are you doing?

23:58.562 --> 23:59.729
[in Australian accent]
Hello, this is Dustin,

23:59.813 --> 24:02.816
and this is the secretary and treasurer
of Hawkins Middle AV Club.

24:02.899 --> 24:05.068
Do you eat kangaroos for breakfast?

24:05.152 --> 24:07.154
- [Mike laughs]
- [knock on door]

24:07.237 --> 24:12.075
Sorry to interrupt, but, uh, may I borrow
Michael, Lucas and Dustin?

24:14.327 --> 24:15.829
[overlapping chatter]

24:17.080 --> 24:18.623
Okay, okay, okay.

24:18.707 --> 24:21.668
One at a time, all right?
You.

24:22.627 --> 24:24.379
- You said he takes what?
- Mirkwood.

24:24.462 --> 24:27.048
- Mirkwood?
- Yeah.

24:27.132 --> 24:30.635
- Have you ever heard of Mirkwood?
- I have not. That sounds made up to me.

24:30.719 --> 24:32.512
No, it's from Lord of the Rings.

24:32.596 --> 24:35.473
- Well, The Hobbit.
- It doesn't matter.

24:35.557 --> 24:37.392
- He asked!
- [mockingly] "He asked!"

24:37.475 --> 24:39.060
- [Mike] Shut up, guys!
- Hey, hey, hey!

24:39.186 --> 24:41.104
- What'd I just say?
- Shut up.

24:41.188 --> 24:44.482
One at a damn time.
You.

24:44.566 --> 24:47.777
Mirkwood, it's a real road.
It's just the name that's made up.

24:47.861 --> 24:49.237
It's where Cornwallis and Kerley meet.

24:49.321 --> 24:51.823
- Yeah, all right, I think I know that--
- We can show you, if you want.

24:51.907 --> 24:53.241
I said that I know it!

24:53.325 --> 24:55.243
- We can help look.
- Yeah.

24:55.327 --> 24:57.245
- No.
- [boys clamoring]

24:57.329 --> 25:00.457
No.
After school, you are all to go home.

25:00.540 --> 25:01.750
Immediately.

25:01.833 --> 25:05.629
That means no biking around looking
for your friend, no investigating,

25:05.712 --> 25:06.796
no nonsense.

25:06.880 --> 25:08.840
This isn't some Lord of the Rings book.

25:08.924 --> 25:11.718
- The Hobbit.
- Shut up!

25:11.801 --> 25:13.178
- Hey!
- [Mike] Stop it!

25:13.261 --> 25:14.387
[boys bickering]

25:14.471 --> 25:16.389
[softly] Do I make myself clear?

25:21.603 --> 25:26.149
Do I make myself... clear?

25:27.150 --> 25:28.944
[Mike and Dustin] Yes, sir.
[Lucas] Yeah.

25:40.789 --> 25:42.499
Ring-a-ding-ding!

25:42.582 --> 25:44.292
Anybody home?

25:44.376 --> 25:46.002
[Will] Password?

25:46.086 --> 25:48.046
Uh, Rada...

25:49.381 --> 25:51.883
[stammering] Radaga-- Radagast?

25:51.967 --> 25:54.386
[Will] Yeah. You may enter.

25:54.469 --> 25:56.930
[Joyce] Thank you, sir.

25:57.931 --> 25:59.557
So, guess what?

25:59.641 --> 26:02.102
I got off early and...

26:02.185 --> 26:04.854
Ta-da!
Poltergeist.

26:04.938 --> 26:06.481
I... I thought I wasn't allowed to see it.

26:06.564 --> 26:07.941
I changed my mind.

26:08.984 --> 26:10.819
As long as you don't have nightmares
for a week.

26:10.902 --> 26:13.405
No, I won't.
I don't get scared like that anymore.

26:13.488 --> 26:14.489
Oh, yeah?

26:14.572 --> 26:16.241
Not even of clowns?

26:16.324 --> 26:17.409
No.

26:17.492 --> 26:19.869
What about my witch?

26:19.953 --> 26:21.371
- No. Mom...
- Ooh...

26:21.454 --> 26:23.290
- I'm not five anymore.
- But Will Byers...

26:23.373 --> 26:25.834
- I'm going to cook you up in my--
- Stop. That's so stupid. Mom!

26:27.961 --> 26:29.129
[sighs]

26:30.171 --> 26:31.298
[Jonathan] Will?

26:31.381 --> 26:32.966
- [shouting] Will?
- Will?

26:34.509 --> 26:35.760
Will?

26:38.722 --> 26:40.307
- Will?
- Will!

26:41.641 --> 26:43.101
- [Jonathan] Will!
- Will?

26:43.184 --> 26:44.728
[Joyce] Will!

26:44.811 --> 26:46.479
Where are you?

26:55.864 --> 26:57.073
Geez.

26:57.949 --> 26:59.701
Your parents forget to feed you?

27:03.371 --> 27:05.206
Is that why you ran away?

27:08.668 --> 27:09.878
They, uh...

27:10.879 --> 27:12.047
They hurt you?

27:14.924 --> 27:16.634
You went to the hospital, you got scared,

27:16.718 --> 27:18.386
you ran off, you wound up here,
is that it?

27:21.431 --> 27:22.640
All right.

27:24.476 --> 27:27.854
I'll give this back, all right?
And you can have as much as you want.

27:28.521 --> 27:29.939
All right?
Maybe even some ice cream.

27:30.023 --> 27:32.108
But you gotta answer
a few of my questions first, all right?

27:33.568 --> 27:35.445
We got a deal?

27:37.322 --> 27:41.076
All right, let's start
with the easy stuff. All right?

27:41.159 --> 27:44.537
My name's Benny.
Benny Hammond.

27:44.621 --> 27:46.331
See? Like this. Here.

27:46.414 --> 27:49.334
I got you.
Don't worry. It's okay.

27:49.417 --> 27:52.879
Nice to meet you, yeah.
And you are?

27:55.465 --> 27:57.008
[sighing]

27:59.761 --> 28:01.262
[sighs]

28:02.222 --> 28:03.264
Eleven?

28:04.307 --> 28:05.600
What's that mean?

28:06.476 --> 28:08.228
What's it mean?

28:09.312 --> 28:11.564
- No.
- Well, I'll be damned.

28:11.648 --> 28:13.358
She speaks.

28:13.441 --> 28:15.110
"No"? No, what?

28:16.820 --> 28:19.906
[clicks tongue] All right.
I guess no more food, then.

28:19.989 --> 28:21.157
Eleven.

28:22.534 --> 28:23.576
Yeah.

28:24.911 --> 28:26.454
What's it mean?

28:28.206 --> 28:29.624
Eleven.

28:31.334 --> 28:33.503
All right, then.

28:33.586 --> 28:35.338
[chuckles] Here you go.

28:35.422 --> 28:37.173
Take it easy, take it easy.

28:38.425 --> 28:39.467
[sighs]

28:39.551 --> 28:42.178
Yeah, look, all I know
is that she's scared to death.

28:42.262 --> 28:44.389
Yeah, I think
maybe she's been abused or...

28:44.472 --> 28:46.099
kidnapped or something.

28:47.600 --> 28:50.186
Yeah, it'd be great
if someone would come by.

28:50.270 --> 28:54.733
Yeah, we're at 4819 Randolph Lane.
Yeah, Randolph.

28:54.816 --> 28:56.609
[fan rattling]

29:02.741 --> 29:04.492
[rattling continues]

29:08.329 --> 29:09.456
[rattling intensifies]

29:21.634 --> 29:23.386
[Callahan] Will Byers?

29:26.181 --> 29:27.557
[Powell yelling] Will!

29:28.808 --> 29:31.060
[Callahan] Will Byers?

29:31.144 --> 29:32.687
[hooting]

29:34.063 --> 29:36.065
Come on, kid!

29:36.149 --> 29:37.400
[Powell] Will?

29:38.526 --> 29:42.322
- [Powell whistles]
- Hey! I got something.

29:49.370 --> 29:52.290
- That his bike?
- Yeah, he must have crashed.

29:53.583 --> 29:55.210
[Callahan] You think
he got hurt in the fall?

29:56.085 --> 29:57.629
Not so hurt he couldn't walk away.

29:57.712 --> 29:59.631
Bike like this is like
a Cadillac to these kids.

29:59.714 --> 30:01.341
He would've walked it home.

30:08.890 --> 30:10.433
[static]

30:10.517 --> 30:12.227
[radio frequencies tuning]

30:12.352 --> 30:13.311
[woman 1] ...get off work if I win.

30:13.394 --> 30:15.063
[woman 2] Oh, Friday I'm supposed to...

30:15.146 --> 30:17.941
[woman 3] ...but we will cover
whatever the damages are to your property.

30:18.024 --> 30:19.692
- It's just, um...
- [woman 4] That's for sure.

30:19.776 --> 30:22.403
- [overlapping conversations]
- [line ringing]

30:29.035 --> 30:30.203
[Joyce] Is Lonnie there?

30:30.286 --> 30:32.580
[woman] Lonnie isn't here right now.
[Joyce] Can you please--

30:32.664 --> 30:34.541
- I told you, Lonnie's not here.
- Who is this?

30:34.624 --> 30:36.626
- His girlfriend, Cynthia.
- Cynthia.

30:36.709 --> 30:39.420
- Who the hell is this?
- Cynthia, this is Joyce.

30:39.504 --> 30:41.256
- Who?
- Lonnie's ex-wife.

30:41.339 --> 30:43.383
- I really need to speak to him--
- Lonnie's not here.

30:43.466 --> 30:45.343
- Can you please put-- No!
- Why don't you call back later?

30:45.426 --> 30:46.636
No, not later. Now!

30:46.719 --> 30:47.887
- Can--
- [line disconnects]

30:47.971 --> 30:49.389
- Bitch!
- [Jonathan] Mom.

30:49.472 --> 30:51.933
- What?
- You have to stay calm.

30:52.016 --> 30:53.351
[chuckles]

30:56.354 --> 30:57.438
[Joyce muttering]

30:58.565 --> 31:00.608
[phone ringing]

31:00.692 --> 31:01.734
[Lonnie] Hey, you've reached Lonnie.

31:01.818 --> 31:04.028
Leave a message
and I'll holler right back at ya.

31:04.112 --> 31:07.866
Lonnie, some teenager just hung up on me.

31:07.949 --> 31:10.451
Will is... is missing.
I don't know where he is.

31:10.535 --> 31:11.703
[voice breaking] I need...

31:11.786 --> 31:14.372
I just need you to call me back,
please, just--

31:14.455 --> 31:16.958
- [answering machine beeps]
- [line disconnects]

31:17.041 --> 31:18.793
- Damn it! Damn it!
- [car approaching]

31:18.877 --> 31:20.545
- [sighs deeply]
- Mom?

31:20.628 --> 31:21.629
What?

31:23.673 --> 31:24.841
Cops.

31:39.689 --> 31:43.234
- It was just lying there?
- Yeah. Cal?

31:44.152 --> 31:47.822
- Did it have any blood on it, or--
- No, no, no, no, no...

31:47.906 --> 31:49.407
Phil?

31:49.490 --> 31:51.910
If you found the bike out there,
why are you here?

31:52.952 --> 31:55.830
- Well, he had a key to the house, right?
- [Jonathan] Yeah.

31:56.831 --> 31:58.249
So...

31:59.208 --> 32:00.376
maybe he came home.

32:00.460 --> 32:02.503
[stammers] You think I didn't check
my own house?

32:02.587 --> 32:04.380
I'm not saying that.

32:05.298 --> 32:08.051
- Has this always been here?
- [Joyce] What? I don't know.

32:08.134 --> 32:10.970
Probably. I mean, I have two boys.
Look at this place.

32:12.597 --> 32:13.765
You're not sure?

32:13.848 --> 32:15.934
- [Joyce sighs]
- [dog barking]

32:18.478 --> 32:19.854
[barks]

32:25.735 --> 32:26.736
Hey.

32:28.279 --> 32:30.114
Hey, what's up with this guy, huh?

32:30.198 --> 32:32.700
Nothing, he's probably just hungry.
Come on.

33:31.968 --> 33:34.012
[indistinct squelching]

33:38.641 --> 33:40.309
[squelching stops]

33:51.654 --> 33:53.322
- [Callahan] Hey!
- Jesus!

33:53.406 --> 33:55.992
What are you, deaf?
I've been calling you.

33:56.075 --> 33:58.536
- [exhales]
- What's going on?

34:00.705 --> 34:01.831
Hello?

34:01.914 --> 34:05.001
- Are you sure you're okay, Chief?
- Listen, I want you to call Flo.

34:05.084 --> 34:06.419
I want to get
a search party together, all right?

34:06.502 --> 34:09.630
All the volunteers she can muster.
Bring flashlights, too.

34:09.714 --> 34:12.008
[Callahan] Hey, you think
we got a problem here?

34:19.057 --> 34:21.809
[Mike] We should be out there right now.
We should be helping look for him.

34:21.893 --> 34:23.770
We've been over this, Mike.
The chief says--

34:23.853 --> 34:25.354
- I don't care what the chief said.
- Michael!

34:25.438 --> 34:27.106
We have to do something.
Will can be in danger.

34:27.190 --> 34:28.399
More reason to stay put.

34:28.483 --> 34:30.526
- Mom!
- End of discussion.

34:34.739 --> 34:38.659
So... me and Barbara are gonna
study at her house tonight.

34:38.743 --> 34:41.162
- That's cool, right?
- No, not cool.

34:41.245 --> 34:42.497
What? Why not?

34:42.580 --> 34:45.792
Why do you think?
Am I speaking Chinese in this house?

34:45.875 --> 34:48.920
Until we know Will is okay, no one leaves.

34:49.003 --> 34:50.797
- This is such bullshit.
- Language.

34:50.880 --> 34:52.298
So we're under house arrest?

34:52.381 --> 34:54.300
Just because Mike's friend got lost
on the way home from...

34:54.383 --> 34:56.677
- Wait, this is Will's fault?
- Nancy, take that back.

34:56.761 --> 34:58.304
- No!
- You're just pissed off

34:58.387 --> 35:00.348
'cause you wanna hang out with Steve.

35:01.974 --> 35:03.226
- Steve?
- Who is Steve?

35:03.309 --> 35:05.728
- Her new boyfriend.
- You are such a douchebag, Mike!

35:05.812 --> 35:07.605
- Language!
- [groans]

35:09.273 --> 35:10.691
Nancy, come back.

35:11.526 --> 35:12.777
Come back!

35:12.860 --> 35:16.280
[sighs] It's okay. It's okay, Holly.
Here, have some juice, okay?

35:16.989 --> 35:18.032
You see, Michael?

35:18.116 --> 35:20.409
- You see what happens?
- [shouting] What happens when what?

35:20.493 --> 35:24.080
I'm the only one acting normal here!
I'm the only one that cares about Will!

35:24.163 --> 35:26.207
That is really unfair, son.

35:26.290 --> 35:27.500
We care.

35:30.503 --> 35:32.296
[sighs]

35:32.380 --> 35:34.173
- Mike!
- Let him go.

35:36.884 --> 35:39.303
I hope you're enjoying your chicken, Ted.

35:40.054 --> 35:41.597
What did I do?

35:43.933 --> 35:46.519
Hey! What'd I do?

35:49.564 --> 35:51.607
[boy] Will!
[man 1] Will Byers!

35:51.691 --> 35:52.733
[man 2] Will!

35:52.817 --> 35:54.652
[woman] Will, we're here for you, bud!

35:54.735 --> 35:56.529
[volunteers shouting indistinctly]

35:57.530 --> 35:59.740
[Mr. Clarke] He's a good student.

35:59.824 --> 36:03.244
- [Hopper] What?
- Will. He's a good student.

36:03.327 --> 36:04.954
Great one, actually.

36:05.454 --> 36:07.373
I don't think we've met.
Scott Clarke.

36:07.456 --> 36:10.751
Teacher, Hawkins Middle.
Earth and biology.

36:10.835 --> 36:12.837
[Hopper] I always had
a distaste for science.

36:12.920 --> 36:14.881
[Mr. Clarke] Well, maybe you had
a bad teacher.

36:14.964 --> 36:17.300
[Hopper] Yeah, Ms. Ratliff
was a piece of work.

36:17.383 --> 36:20.011
[Mr. Clarke chuckles] Ratliff?
You bet.

36:20.094 --> 36:22.263
She's still kicking around,
believe it or not.

36:22.346 --> 36:26.142
[Hopper] Oh, I believe it.
Mummies never die, so they tell me.

36:26.767 --> 36:28.269
Sarah, my daughter...

36:29.645 --> 36:33.816
Galaxies, the universe, whatnot...
She always understood all that stuff.

36:33.900 --> 36:36.360
I always figured there was enough
going on down here,

36:36.444 --> 36:38.196
I never needed to look elsewhere.

36:38.738 --> 36:40.489
[Mr. Clarke] Your daughter,
what grade is she?

36:40.573 --> 36:43.367
- Maybe I'll get her in my class.
- No, she, uh...

36:43.451 --> 36:45.995
She lives with her mom in the city.

36:46.078 --> 36:49.540
Thanks for coming out, Teach.
We really appreciate it.

36:51.751 --> 36:54.629
- She died a few years back.
- Sorry?

36:54.712 --> 36:55.963
His kid.

37:08.434 --> 37:09.977
Lucas, do you copy?
It's Mike.

37:10.061 --> 37:12.897
- Lucas?
- Hey, it's Lucas.

37:12.980 --> 37:13.981
I know it's you.

37:14.065 --> 37:17.235
And say "over" when you're done talking
so I know when you're done. Over.

37:17.318 --> 37:18.945
I'm done. Over.

37:19.028 --> 37:21.447
I'm worried about Will. Over.

37:21.530 --> 37:23.574
[sighs] Yeah.

37:25.409 --> 37:27.328
This is crazy. Over.

37:27.411 --> 37:29.038
I was thinking...

37:30.539 --> 37:33.376
Will could've cast Protection last night,
but he didn't.

37:33.459 --> 37:34.460
He cast Fireball.

37:34.543 --> 37:38.297
- Over.
- What's your point? Over.

37:38.381 --> 37:43.094
My point is... he could've played it safe,
but he didn't.

37:43.177 --> 37:45.054
He put himself in danger
to help the party.

37:45.137 --> 37:46.264
Over.

37:49.058 --> 37:51.477
Meet me in ten.
Over and out.

38:09.412 --> 38:11.414
[pop music playing on radio]

38:13.582 --> 38:15.376
[tapping on window]

38:22.300 --> 38:23.301
[whispers] What are you doing here?

38:23.384 --> 38:25.678
I told you on the phone,
I'm under house arrest now.

38:25.761 --> 38:28.597
- I figured we'd just study here.
- No. No way.

38:28.681 --> 38:30.933
Oh, come on.
I can't have you failing this test.

38:31.017 --> 38:32.810
So just... bear with me.

38:32.893 --> 38:34.186
[window rattles]

38:35.855 --> 38:36.856
What'd I tell you?

38:38.274 --> 38:39.400
Ninja.

38:40.943 --> 38:42.028
[scoffs]

38:43.487 --> 38:44.989
[hose running]

38:53.456 --> 38:54.915
You like that ice cream, huh?

38:56.167 --> 38:57.585
Smile looks good on you.

38:58.419 --> 39:00.004
You know, smile?

39:02.548 --> 39:05.885
- [chuckles]
- [music playing faintly on radio]

39:05.968 --> 39:07.303
[knocking on door]

39:09.013 --> 39:10.765
All right.
You just sit tight.

39:10.848 --> 39:14.226
Whoever it is, I'll tell 'em to go away
real quick, all right?

39:16.437 --> 39:19.106
- [knocking continues]
- Yeah, yeah, yeah...

39:20.232 --> 39:22.735
- Hey, can I help you?
- Hi, you must be Benny Hammond.

39:22.818 --> 39:25.071
I'm afraid I am. I'm afraid
we're closed for the evening, too.

39:25.154 --> 39:27.907
- So try back tomorrow morning.
- Connie Frazier. Social Services.

39:27.990 --> 39:30.868
Ah, Social Services. My apologies.
I didn't expect you so soon.

39:30.951 --> 39:33.788
- That's a heck of a drive.
- Not too bad this time of night.

39:33.871 --> 39:36.123
Hey, listen, I...
I haven't told her that you're coming yet.

39:36.207 --> 39:40.169
I didn't want her running off again.
She's a tad skittish.

39:40.252 --> 39:42.880
- Children I work with usually are.
- Right, right.

39:43.464 --> 39:46.300
- So, where is she?
- Right. She's in the kitchen.

39:46.384 --> 39:48.219
- Come on up. I'll introduce you.
- Thank you.

39:48.302 --> 39:50.096
Sorry again for trying
to turn you away there.

39:50.179 --> 39:51.222
- It's fine.
- You know, it's funny.

39:51.305 --> 39:53.724
- Your, uh, voice sounds different on the--
- [silenced gunshot]

39:56.560 --> 39:57.686
[gasps]

39:57.770 --> 39:59.063
[dish clattering]

40:03.526 --> 40:05.611
- [static]
- [radio scrambling]

40:05.694 --> 40:07.238
- [loud thud]
- [men groan]

40:07.321 --> 40:09.323
[radio resumes playing]

40:24.547 --> 40:27.466
[Lucas] Ah, man.
This is it.

40:32.054 --> 40:33.055
[sighs]

40:33.722 --> 40:35.141
[thunder rumbling]

40:36.225 --> 40:38.060
Hey, guys.
You feel that?

40:41.105 --> 40:42.773
- I think maybe we should go back.
- No.

40:42.857 --> 40:45.484
We're not going back.
Just stay close.

40:45.568 --> 40:46.694
Come on.

40:47.820 --> 40:51.157
Just stay on channel six.
Don't do anything stupid.

40:54.577 --> 40:55.744
[thunder rumbling]

40:55.828 --> 40:57.163
Hey, guys, wait up.

40:57.705 --> 40:59.123
Wait up!

41:05.004 --> 41:07.798
[Steve] "Which polymers occur naturally?"

41:09.216 --> 41:11.677
Starch and cellulose.

41:11.760 --> 41:13.012
Mmm.

41:13.095 --> 41:17.349
"In a molecule of CH4,
the hydrogen atoms are spatially oriented

41:17.433 --> 41:19.894
- towards the centers of--"
- Tetrahedrons.

41:19.977 --> 41:22.480
Wow.
Jesus, how many of these did you make?

41:22.563 --> 41:24.398
You said you wanted to help.

41:25.441 --> 41:26.650
How about this? How about...

41:26.734 --> 41:28.277
How about every time
that you get something right,

41:28.360 --> 41:29.862
I have to take off
an item of clothing.

41:29.945 --> 41:31.530
But every time
that you get something wrong--

41:31.614 --> 41:32.823
- Uh, pass.
- Oh, come on.

41:32.907 --> 41:33.949
- Come on.
- No.

41:34.033 --> 41:35.409
- Come on. It'll be fun.
- No.

41:35.493 --> 41:36.869
"During fractional distillation,

41:36.952 --> 41:39.622
hydrocarbons are separated
according to their--"

41:39.705 --> 41:40.748
Melting point.

41:42.208 --> 41:44.376
Ooh, it's boiling points.

41:44.460 --> 41:45.878
That's what I meant.

41:45.961 --> 41:47.963
Yeah, that's not what you said.

41:48.881 --> 41:50.674
- No.
- No?

41:51.550 --> 41:53.886
Oh, do you need...
Do you need help, or...

41:53.969 --> 41:55.012
No.

42:16.534 --> 42:18.160
[whispers] Steve.
Steve, come on.

42:18.244 --> 42:19.245
What?

42:19.328 --> 42:21.455
Are you crazy?
My parents are here.

42:23.165 --> 42:25.668
That's weird, I... don't see them.

42:29.505 --> 42:34.176
Was this your plan all along?
To... to get in my room and then...

42:34.260 --> 42:36.845
- get another notch on your belt.
- No. Nancy, no.

42:36.929 --> 42:39.056
I'm not Laurie, or Amy, or Becky.

42:39.139 --> 42:40.724
You mean, you're not a slut.

42:41.559 --> 42:42.643
That's not what I'm saying.

42:42.726 --> 42:44.478
You know, you're so cute when you lie.

42:44.979 --> 42:46.230
Shut up.

42:49.108 --> 42:50.484
Bad Steve.

42:50.568 --> 42:54.113
[groans] Bad.
Don't do that to Miss Nancy...

42:54.697 --> 42:56.740
You're an idiot, Steve Harrington.

42:57.658 --> 42:59.702
You are beautiful, Nancy Wheeler.

43:04.623 --> 43:06.041
[Steve grunts]

43:06.125 --> 43:08.711
"Compared to the rate
of inorganic reactions,

43:08.794 --> 43:12.548
the rate of organic reactions
is generally..."

43:12.631 --> 43:14.091
- [thunder rumbling]
- [rain falling]

43:15.551 --> 43:18.596
[Joyce] Jonathan, wow.
You took these?

43:19.513 --> 43:21.015
These are great.

43:22.141 --> 43:25.102
[sniffling] Wow, they really are.

43:26.270 --> 43:29.356
I know I haven't been there for you.
[stammers] I've been...

43:29.440 --> 43:31.525
working so hard and I...

43:31.609 --> 43:33.444
I just feel bad.
I don't even...

43:33.527 --> 43:35.988
barely know what's going on with you.
[chuckles]

43:36.071 --> 43:38.824
All right?
I am sorry about that.

43:39.992 --> 43:41.201
[Jonathan sobs softly]

43:42.202 --> 43:43.495
Hey, what is it?

43:44.413 --> 43:45.748
What is it, honey?

43:47.499 --> 43:49.918
- Nothing. [sniffles]
- Tell me. Tell me.

43:50.002 --> 43:52.046
- Come on. You can...
- No.

43:52.129 --> 43:53.297
It's just...

43:54.506 --> 43:56.300
[voice breaking]
I should've been there for him.

43:56.383 --> 43:59.386
[hoarsely] No. Oh, no.
You can't do that to yourself.

43:59.470 --> 44:02.681
This was not your fault.
Do you hear me?

44:02.765 --> 44:06.435
He is... close.
I know it. [stammers] I...

44:07.102 --> 44:09.813
I feel it in my heart.
[sniffles]

44:10.564 --> 44:13.359
You just have to...
You have to trust me on this, okay?

44:13.442 --> 44:14.693
[sniffles]

44:16.111 --> 44:17.780
- Yeah.
- Oh, look at this.

44:17.863 --> 44:20.240
Look at this one.
Look at this one.

44:20.324 --> 44:21.659
[both laugh]

44:22.576 --> 44:24.745
- I mean, that's it, right?
- Yeah.

44:24.828 --> 44:26.622
[hoarsely] That's it.
That's the one.

44:26.705 --> 44:28.165
- [sighs]
- [phone ringing]

44:30.209 --> 44:33.128
- Hello?
- [static on phone]

44:33.212 --> 44:34.838
- Hello?
- [static continues]

44:34.922 --> 44:35.964
Lonnie?

44:36.048 --> 44:37.800
- Dad?
- Hopper?

44:37.883 --> 44:39.927
- [muffled breathing on phone]
- Who is this?

44:40.010 --> 44:41.845
[breathing continues]

44:43.222 --> 44:44.264
Will?

44:45.140 --> 44:46.225
- Will?
- It's Will?

44:46.308 --> 44:48.977
- [scrambled voice chitters]
- [static]

44:49.061 --> 44:50.437
- [sobs]
- Mom, it's Will?

44:51.438 --> 44:52.856
- [yelling] Who is this?
- [indistinct growling]

44:52.940 --> 44:55.067
- [yelling] What have you done to my boy?
- What? What?

44:55.150 --> 44:56.652
Give me back my son!

44:56.735 --> 44:58.529
- [electricity surges]
- [screams]

44:58.612 --> 45:00.447
- [groans]
- Hello?

45:00.531 --> 45:01.782
Hello, who is this?

45:01.865 --> 45:04.618
- Hello? Who is this?
- [sobbing]

45:04.701 --> 45:07.162
- Mom, who was it? Who was it, Mom?
- [muttering incoherently]

45:07.246 --> 45:08.914
- [sobbing] It was him.
- Look at me, Mom. Was it Will?

45:08.997 --> 45:10.207
- Yes.
- What did he say?

45:10.290 --> 45:12.418
[sobbing] He just breathed.
He just breathed.

45:12.501 --> 45:14.461
- [Jonathan] And was someone else there?
- I...

45:14.545 --> 45:17.256
- Mom, who was there? Who was it?
- It was him.

45:17.339 --> 45:20.050
I know it was his breathing.
I know it was his breathing.

45:20.134 --> 45:21.260
[sobbing]

45:21.343 --> 45:22.719
- [thunder rumbling]
- [Mike] Will!

45:23.720 --> 45:26.223
- Will!
- [Lucas] Byers!

45:26.306 --> 45:29.059
[Dustin] I've got your X-Men 134!

45:29.810 --> 45:31.895
Guys, I really think
we should turn back.

45:31.979 --> 45:33.230
[Lucas] Seriously, Dustin?

45:33.313 --> 45:35.607
You wanna be a baby,
then go home already!

45:35.691 --> 45:37.401
I'm just being realistic, Lucas!

45:37.484 --> 45:39.486
No, you're just being a big sissy!

45:40.112 --> 45:43.490
[Dustin] Did you ever think Will went
missing because he ran into something bad?

45:43.574 --> 45:46.452
And we're going to the exact same spot
where he was last seen?

45:46.535 --> 45:49.371
- And we have no weapons or anything?
- Dustin, shut up.

45:49.455 --> 45:51.457
I'm just saying,
does that seem smart to you?

45:51.540 --> 45:53.667
- Shut up. Shut up.
- [rustling]

45:53.750 --> 45:55.419
Did you guys hear that?

45:55.502 --> 45:57.880
- [rustling]
- [indistinct screeching]

45:59.214 --> 46:00.591
- [rustling]
- [boys gasp]

46:17.983 --> 46:19.985
[theme music playing]
